{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "notes": "Added automatic background logging (auto_log.py): the boat now logs itself to Power_Log/GPS_Log on a schedule, not just on a manual 'Log Now' press -- frequent (every 5 min) while mode == 'key_on' (engine running), much less frequent (every 60 min) otherwise, with an immediate log the moment the engine starts rather than waiting out whatever's left of the previous, longer docked interval. Runs from ble_service.py's existing run() loop (checked every ~2s tick) -- does NOT run while the Wi-Fi AP fallback console is active, since field_console.py's serve() loop blocks on a plain socket accept with no periodic hook. Reports outcomes via command_result ('auto_logged (power: ..., gps: ...)') same as a manual log. Also de-duplicated the actual Power_Log+GPS_Log logging logic: ble_service.py's manual 'log' command, this new auto-log trigger, and field_console.py's web Log Now page all now share one function (ble_service.log_power_and_gps()) instead of three separate near-identical copies.",
